  ('Bachelor of Quantity Surveying', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Universiti Malaya (UM)' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 4521, '3.5 years', '["Mar","Oct"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Quantity Surveying program at Universiti Malaya (UM), initiated in 1995, is designed to equip graduates with a professional degree to practice in the construction industry, both locally and internationally. The program emphasizes the effective application of knowledge, with a strong awareness of cultural and ethical considerations.

Accredited by prominent bodies such as the Board of Quantity Surveyors Malaysia (BQSM) and the Royal Institution of Chartered Surveyors (RICS) in the United Kingdom, the program enjoys recognition that enhances its reputation. This accreditation ensures that graduates have access to a wide range of employment opportunities across the region and globally.

The program comprises a 3½ year full-time study period, and upon successful completion, students are awarded a Bachelor’s Degree in Quantity Surveying, preparing them for successful careers in the field.

- National Higher School Certificate (or an Advanced Level equivalent) with the grade 80% and above.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., UEC, Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["Consultant QS practices\nConstruction companies\nClaim and contract specialist\nDispute resolution experts,\nClaim consultants\nDevelopers,\nBanking sector\nInsurance companies,\nOil and gas industry,\nGovernment agencies and authorities"]'::jsonb, 'Free', '- National Higher School Certificate (or an Advanced Level equivalent) with the grade 80% and above.

