  ('Bachelor of Science Statistics', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Universiti Malaya (UM)' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 3036, '4 years', '["Mar","Oct"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Science in Statistics program at Universiti Malaya UM is a four-year course that offers exceptional training in both the theory and practice of mathematical statistics This comprehensive program covers key areas such as inferential statistics, modeling techniques, and the essential skills for interpreting and reporting statistical analyses

Graduates of this program are equipped with a solid foundation to apply statistical methods to solve real-world problems The curriculum supports a shift towards analyzing real-world data using modern statistical techniques and promotes a data-driven culture, ensuring that students are well-prepared for careers in various industries where data analysis is vital.

- National Higher School Certificate (or an Advanced Level equivalent) with the grade 80% and above.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., UEC, Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

