  ('Bachelor of Biomedical Engineering', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Universiti Malaya (UM)' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 5572, '4 years', '["Mar","Oct"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Biomedical Engineering program at Universiti Malaya (UM) is designed to bridge the gap between engineering and medical sciences. This interdisciplinary program equips students with the knowledge and skills needed to develop innovative solutions for healthcare challenges.

Students will learn about the principles of engineering, biology, and medicine, applying this knowledge to design medical devices, diagnostic equipment, and rehabilitation technologies. The curriculum emphasizes hands-on experience through laboratory work and projects, fostering critical thinking and problem-solving skills.

Graduates of this program will be prepared to contribute significantly to the healthcare industry, improving patient care and advancing medical technologies. With the increasing demand for biomedical engineers, this degree opens up diverse career opportunities in hospitals, research institutions, and the medical device industry.

- National Higher School Certificate (or an Advanced Level equivalent) with the grade 80% and above.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., UEC, Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["Biomedical Engineer\nBiomedical Equipment Engineer\nMedical Science Officer\nResearcher"]'::jsonb, 'Free', '- National Higher School Certificate (or an Advanced Level equivalent) with the grade 80% and above.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., UEC, Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.'),
  ('Bachelor of Biomedical Science', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Universiti Malaya (UM)' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 7073, '4 years', '["Mar","Oct"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Biomedical Science program at Universiti Malaya (UM) provides comprehensive knowledge and training in medical science, emphasizing healthcare and research Students enroll in the program for a minimum of four years, with a structured curriculum designed to build a strong foundation in biomedical disciplines

In the first year, students are introduced to the basics of medical sciences, gaining fundamental knowledge about human body structure, functions, and mechanisms By the second year, they delve deeper into specific biomedical fields such as Histopathology, Haematology, Chemical Pathology, and Infectious Diseases, while also understanding the impact of diseases and pathology

Practical sessions will help students develop confidence and skills in laboratory medicine, and an Industrial Training attachment in the third year will provide valuable exposure to real-world biomedical services Returning for their final year, students will undertake their most significant milestone: conducting independent research projects in their chosen area of interest, solidifying their expertise and preparing them for careers in biomedical science.

For qualifications and certificates (e.g., UEC, Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

Biomedical Science graduates from Universiti Malaya are confident, skilled, ambitious, and prepared for their professional journeys. Career opportunities are diverse and include:', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["Biomedical Science graduates from Universiti Malaya are confident, skilled, ambitious, and prepared for their professional journeys. Career opportunities are diverse and include:\n\nClinical Laboratory Service Departments\nTeaching Institutions\nResearch Centres (public and private sectors)\n\nBiomedical Scientists can take on responsible roles in:\n\nHealthcare Teams:\n\nFocused on patient care\nInvolved in basic and applied clinical research\n\n\n\nResearch Teams:\n\nAllied medical disciplines\nFood and pharmaceutical industries\nPublic health\nBiotechnology\n\nAdditionally, post-graduate training is strongly encouraged, both domestically and internationally, to enhance the quality of biomedical science and improve healthcare and welfare for all."]'::jsonb, 'Free', 'For qualifications and certificates (e.g., UEC, Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.'),
  ('Bachelor of Building Surveying', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Universiti Malaya (UM)' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 4576, '3.5 years', '["Mar","Oct"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Building Surveying program at Universiti Malaya (UM) addresses the growing demand for professional Building Surveyors in Malaysia, offering essential services in various economic and development contexts. The scope of Building Surveying encompasses all stages of a development project, from initial planning and construction management to maintenance and the conservation of historically significant buildings.

Established in 1996, this program aims to produce ethical and professional Building Surveyors and Property Managers equipped to navigate technological and managerial challenges both nationally and internationally. The curriculum is accredited by notable professional bodies, including the Royal Institution of Surveyors Malaysia (RISM) and the Royal Institution of Chartered Surveyors (RICS) in the UK.

The minimum study duration for the Bachelor of Building Surveying is 3½ years. Graduates of the program will earn a Bachelor’s Degree in Building Surveying, positioning them for successful careers in the construction and property industry.

- National Higher School Certificate (or an Advanced Level equivalent) with the grade 80% and above.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., UEC, Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["Building Surveyor\nGovernment / Local Authority Surveyor\nFacilities Manager\nProperty Manager\nSite Engineer\nConstruction Manager / Contractor\nEnvironmental Consultant\nGreen Building Facilitator\nProject Manager\nProperty Insurance Adjuster\nBuilding Restoration Specialist / Registered Conservator\nOccupational Safety and Health Officer / Quality Manager\nInfrastructure Asset / Portfolio Manager\nResearcher / Lecturer"]'::jsonb, 'Free', '- National Higher School Certificate (or an Advanced Level equivalent) with the grade 80% and above.

