  ('Bachelor of Civil Engineering', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Universiti Malaya (UM)' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 5407, '4 years', '["Mar","Oct"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Civil Engineering program at Universiti Malaya (UM) provides a robust foundation of knowledge essential for students to apply basic principles in Civil Engineering practice and problem-solving. The curriculum covers various aspects, including the design and construction of projects, financial management, construction process oversight, and maintenance.

This discipline focuses on finding innovative solutions through a blend of creativity and technical knowledge, enabling the planning, design, and execution of critical infrastructure works that enhance the quality of life. Civil engineers contribute significantly to the development of renowned landmarks worldwide, playing a crucial role in addressing the challenges posed by a growing population and the resulting strain on existing infrastructures. As such, civil engineers are vital for improving and constructing the built environment, both now and in the future.

