Our program produces high-caliber graduates equipped for language-related professions across various sectors. In the media, advertising, and publishing industries, graduates can work as journalists, broadcasters, writers, editors, copywriters, and proofreaders. In marketing, banking, and tourism, they may serve as administrators or junior executives. Within corporate communication, roles such as communications officer are available. In the education sector, graduates can become corporate trainers, language teachers, teacher educators, program/curriculum developers, and education managers or administrators in both government and private institutions. Additionally, opportunities exist for those interested in careers as translators and interpreters. This diverse range of career paths underscores the versatility and demand for language professionals.

