  ('Bachelor of Media Studies', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Universiti Malaya (UM)' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 4173, '3 years', '["Mar","Oct"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Media Studies program at Universiti Malaya (UM) is designed to cultivate knowledgeable, technology-literate graduates skilled in producing impactful media content. The program prepares students to contribute effectively to the media and communication field, whether as industry professionals or as scholars.

Offered as a full-time program, it comprises 122 credits, requiring a minimum study duration of 7 semesters plus 1 short semester, with a maximum of 11 semesters. The Bachelor of Media Studies follows a 3u1i structure, combining face-to-face and online classes. Students will complete assignments and an academic project over 5 normal semesters and 1 short semester, followed by 2 semesters of industrial training internships to gain practical experience in the field.

