  ('Bachelor of Nursing Science', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Universiti Malaya (UM)' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 7315, '4 years', '["Oct"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Nursing Science program at Universiti Malaya (UM) is a four-year course designed to prepare graduates for contemporary nursing roles By applying medical and scientific knowledge, students will learn to provide high-quality nursing care to patients Upon completion of the program, graduates will be awarded the Bachelor of Nursing Science degree

Offered by the Department of Nursing Science within the Faculty of Medicine, this program has a rich history The department was established in 1993 as a Nursing Science unit under the Department of Allied Health Sciences, pioneering the transition from advanced diploma to baccalaureate education in nursing in Malaysia In 2007, it was officially recognized as the Department of Nursing Science, emphasizing the importance of advanced nursing education and professional practice in the healthcare sector.

