Research areas include data acquisition, surveying, photogrammetry, global navigation satellite systems (GNSS), location-based services (LBS), laser scanning, cartography, hydrography, and land information management. Through comprehensive research efforts, students will develop the expertise necessary to tackle complex challenges in geospatial engineering and contribute pioneering solutions across various applications.

