  ('Master of Agricultural Mechanisation and Automation By Research Mode', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Universiti Putra Malaysia (UPM)' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 0, '2 years', '["Oct","Mar"]'::jsonb, 'Master of Agricultural Mechanisation and Automation By Research Mode at Universiti Putra Malaysia (UPM) emphasizes research on agricultural mechanisation systems and models within the agriculture and plantation sectors. The program focuses on the design and application of automation technologies, including computers, controllers, sensors, remote sensing, GIS, GPS, and mechatronics in agricultural industries.

Key topics include the advanced design and development of machinery such as bioproduction robots, harvesters, planters, and chemical sprayers for agricultural and plantation operations. Research also explores the impact of automated systems and controllers in bioproduction and greenhouse environments.

Students will delve into machine vision systems, autonomous devices, control algorithms, soil mapping and yield technologies, and smart farming applications. Additional research areas encompass robotic engineering, including automation, navigation, swarm technologies, and assistive robotics, preparing graduates to meet the evolving needs of modern agriculture.

• A Bachelor’s degree in the field or related fields with a minimum CGPA of 2.750 or equivalent, as accepted by the UPM Senate

