Additionally, the program covers structural design and vehicle integration, focusing on body structure design, crash analysis, stress and fatigue assessment, ergonomic design, and composite materials. Research in combustion and pollution focuses on pollution control systems and energy-efficient fuel combustion technologies. Through rigorous study, graduates will be prepared to innovate and address contemporary challenges in the automotive engineering field.

