Students will engage in topics like time series analysis, spatial modeling, extreme value theory, regression techniques, and robust statistics. Additionally, they will explore Bayesian statistics, Monte Carlo Markov Chain methods, and various aspects of reliability analysis, including survival analysis and biostatistics. This comprehensive program equips graduates with the skills to apply statistical methodologies to solve real-world challenges effectively.

