Additionally, the program includes research on photonic materials and sensors crucial for optical communication and medical applications. Emerging research areas also focus on mid-infrared fiber laser sources that operate within the 2000 nm to 3000 nm wavelength range, which have potential applications in eye-safe free-space optical communications, laser range-finding, and bio-photonics. Graduates are prepared to contribute to advancements in applied physics and its technological applications.

