This program encompasses multiple branches of microbiology, including physiology, genetics, biochemistry, molecular biology, ecology, and virology. Students will explore the beneficial roles of microorganisms in industrial processes, such as the production of antibiotics, enzymes, biopolymers for medical applications, and bioremediation of waste. Despite extensive study over the past 400 years, the exact identification and characterization of many microorganisms remain incomplete, highlighting the need for ongoing research. Graduates will be equipped to make significant contributions to the field of microbiology.

