  ('Master of Science in Nutrition By Research Mode', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Universiti Putra Malaysia (UPM)' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 0, '2 years', '["Oct","Mar"]'::jsonb, 'Master of Science in Nutrition By Research Mode at Universiti Putra Malaysia (UPM) emphasizes research across various animal categories, including farm, companion, laboratory, wildlife, and zoo animals, focusing on health and nutritional well-being. Research projects aim to develop feeding and management systems that enhance growth efficiency and overall health while improving the human health attributes of animal products and maintaining environmental quality.

The program addresses a wide spectrum of issues, from applied problems in animal feeding to fundamental scientific inquiries regarding animal growth, production, and health. Key research areas include the impact of nutrition on health, immunity, digestive and metabolic disorders, reproductive performance, bacterial and parasitic diseases, organic toxins, and nutritional stress management. Additional topics include feed evaluation, processing, efficient feeding systems, nutrient requirement determination, precise ration formulation, phase feeding, and the use of feed additives for neonatal, growing, finishing, and breeding animals.

