  ('Master of Veterinary Science in Animal Physiology By Research Mode', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Universiti Putra Malaysia (UPM)' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 0, '2 years', '["Oct","Mar"]'::jsonb, 'The Master of Veterinary Science in Animal Physiology By Research Mode at Universiti Putra Malaysia (UPM) emphasizes the comprehensive study of various physiological aspects, including molecular, behavioral, nutritional, neuronal, and stress physiology. The program focuses on understanding organ and organ system functions, morphological adaptations, and responses to environmental stimuli, with a strong emphasis on metabolism, regulatory control, and the biological processes in living organisms, including metabolomics, nutrigenomics, and lipidomics.

Candidates will investigate critical metabolic and biochemical pathways related to bioenergetics and homeostatic regulation, as well as ligand-receptor interactions in the context of natural products and both communicable and non-communicable diseases using animal models. At the cellular level, research will delve into cellular organization and function, biomembrane properties, cellular communication, signal transduction, and the regulation of cell survival, apoptosis, and neoplasia. This program prepares graduates for advanced research and practical applications in veterinary science and related fields.

• A Bachelor''s degree in Doctor of Veterinary Medicine with a minimum CGPA of 2.75

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Other qualifications equivalent to a Bachelor’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

