Students will engage in research on various aspects of virology, including virus structure, classification, evolution, and the ways viruses infect and replicate within host cells. Additionally, the program examines the interactions between viruses and the immune responses of animals, covering viral disease pathology, isolation techniques, and methods for diagnosing and treating viral infections. Research areas also encompass molecular virology, gene transfer techniques, gene therapy, veterinary vaccines, and antiviral chemotherapy. This degree equips graduates with the expertise needed to address viral challenges in veterinary medicine.

